ARCHITECTURE

This folder documents tam-clam's system architecture: the modules and how
they connect, the data structures, the algorithms, the dependencies, and
the evaluations of other shells that shaped them.


FILES

  principles.md          the design rules every change follows
  data-structures.md     the shell state, tokens, the syntax tree and the
                         arena, as they are built today, and what comes
                         next
  dependencies.md        every library tam-clam uses, why, and which
                         version removes it
  bash-evaluation.md     how bash works; what to take and what not to
                         repeat

  Later phases add their own files here, for example expansion.md and
  jobs.md (P2), line-editor.md and history.md (P3).


KEEPING IT TRUE

  These documents describe the code as it is. A change that alters a
  structure, an algorithm or a dependency updates the matching file in
  the same commit. Where code and document disagree, the code is right
  and the document is a bug.
